RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1687152Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1697251Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1788786Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1799294Z ^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1799997Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1800738Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1801103Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1801458Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1802791Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1803792Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1804133Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1804801Z    if you are ready to continue.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1805145Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1805693Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1806232Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1806735Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1807282Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1807509Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1807953Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1808304Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1808793Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1809323Z    can use Nix.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1809647Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1809773Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1809950Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1810267Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1810717Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1810927Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1811039Z I will:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1811279Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1811478Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1811905Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1812342Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1812761Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1813067Z  - install Nix in /nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1813582Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1814008Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1814400Z    /root
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1819314Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1820220Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1828452Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1829367Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1829934Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1830465Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1831307Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1846817Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1847727Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1856677Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1857704Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1858435Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1858805Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1859098Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1859565Z 
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1859907Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
RSpec	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31	2026-10-14T21:33:29.1860599Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
